From 172edcf8c36be40c58d4746e59c886bab0ce24b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:46:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: record a Board live_claim refusal of a
 run handoff / lifecycle event and restore the local row

The Board (hermes-hub #111, deployed 3b0a4fe6ac) now refuses a non-holder's run handoff (task_runs
status/outcome/ended_at/summary/metadata, a synthesized run included) and lifecycle events (completed,
blocked, ...) with `live_claim`, by the same live-lease rule as the task row. Before it the Board stored
them and the completion landed half applied (t_01a1d5386cb55abf; repair t_01a1d4faf1ecda4b).

push() recorded `live_claim` only for `tasks` rows. Now (kanban_sync_live_claim.py):
- a `task_runs`/`task_events` live_claim is recorded on the card as `sync_rejected`, naming the table
  and row uid (record_rejection also resolves the task of a delta op that omits task_id);
- on a primary board the local row is put back to the Board's: the returned row is applied (the run's
  sync_version cleared so _local_row_is_newer does not skip it), and a row the Board never stored (a
  phantom synthesized run, a `completed` event) is deleted, tombstoned, so reconcile never re-uploads it;
- a shadow board records the refusal and leaves its live rows, as for the task row.

The fake Board mirrors rows.ts rowFence. No wire change: an older client sees only extra final
rejections (test pushes the old shape with task-only handling: nothing applies, nothing stays pending).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_live_claim_child_rows.py (4: primary restore + holder completes
after, phantom run removed and never re-uploaded, shadow path, old wire shape). Sweep of
test_kanban_sync*/test_kanban_remote*/the new file: 63 files, 1460 passed; the one failure
(forbidden_field payload shape) is fixed by keeping the extra keys to live_claim refusals, 29/29 rerun.
